  "findings": [
    "Exact Fireball targeting succeeds in both fixed training cases; observed terminal spell attribution detects the king finisher.",
    "The fixed policy aims its first unopposed Fireball at (9500,1500) instead of target (3500,7500), then misses the goal window.",
    "In the king case the policy wins with other troops; enemy king death is a distinct terminal outcome, not a confirmed spell-finisher goal.",
    "Attack training currently rewards enemy king death separately and Hog damage even inside spell-finisher tasks; this permits an alternative reward route. These two probes do not establish how often that route dominates.",
    "Published train finisher families contain Fireball only; no Zap finisher family is present in train. No existing heldout family was moved or used to choose weights."
  ],
  "scope": "Two paired training-only examples; diagnostic evidence, not a new test score or a training change."
